"ClpB is the Escherichia coli heat shock protein F84.1 (19… | Minicod (https://www.minicod.com/papers/clpb-is-the-escherichia-coli-heat-shock-protein-f84-1-0aecdbc1)\nciteturn17search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 35.3 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Open Access OLX 1991# ClpB is the Escherichia coli heat shock protein F84.1 ... Squires^{Columbia University}, Steen B.\n\nResearch Paper\n\nOpen Access OLX 1991\n\n# ClpB is the Escherichia coli heat shock protein F84.1\n\nCatherine L. Squires^{Columbia University}, Steen B. Pedersen^{Columbia University}, B. Ross^{Columbia University}, Catherine L. Squires^{Columbia University}\n\nJournal of Bacteriology1991-07-0110.1128/jb.173.14.4254-4262.1991\n\nPaper Info\n\nYear\n\n1991\n\nPublished\n\n1991-07-01\n\nVenue\n\nJournal of Bacteriology\n\nSource\n\nOpenAlex\n\nLanguage\n\nEN\n\nVolume\n\n173\n\nIssue\n\n14\n\nPages\n\n4254-4262\n\nType\n\narticle\n\nID\n\nW1908074424\n\nView PDFView on OpenAlexDOI Link\n\n## Abstract\n\nClpB is thought to be involved in proteolysis because of its sequence similarity to the ClpA subunit of the ClpA-ClpP protease. It has recently been shown that ClpP is a heat shock protein. Here we show that ClpB is the Escherichia coli heat shock protein F84.1. The F84.1 protein was overproduced in strains containing the clpB gene on a plasmid and was absent from two-dimensional gels from a clpB null mutation. Besides possessing a slower growth rate at 44 degrees C, the null mutant strain had a higher rate of death at 50 degrees C. We used reverse transcription of in vivo mRNA to show that the clpB gene was expressed from a sigma 32-specific promoter consensus sequence at both 37 and 42 degrees C. We noted that the clpB+ gene also caused the appearance of a second protein spot, F68.5, on two-dimensional gels. This spot was approximately 147 amino acids smaller than F84.1 and most probably is the result of a second translational start on the clpB mRNA. F68.5 can be observed on many published two-dimensional gels of heat-induced E. coli proteins, but the original catalog of 17 heat shock proteins did not include this spot.\n\n## Fields of Study\n\nHeat shock proteins researchProtein Structure and DynamicsEnzyme Structure and Function\n\n## Research context\n\nHeat shock proteins researchProtein Structure and DynamicsEnzyme Structure and FunctionCLPBBiologyEscherichia coliHeat shock proteinMutantMolecular biologyProteaseProteolysisHSPA4GeneHeat shockBiochemistryHsp70Enzyme\n\n## Authors & Affiliations\n\nCatherine L. SquiresColumbia University Columbia University\n\nSteen B. PedersenColumbia University Columbia University\n\nB. RossColumbia University Columbia University\n\nCatherine L. SquiresColumbia University Columbia University\n\n## Identifiers\n\ndoi\n    10.1128/jb.173.14.4254-4262.1991\n\nmag\n    1908074424\n\npmid\n    2066329\n\nopenalex\n    W1908074424\n\n## Cite this paper\n\nAPA\n\nSelect & copy\n\nCatherine L. Squires, Steen B. Pedersen, B. Ross et al. (1991). ClpB is the Escherichia coli heat shock protein F84.1. Journal of Bacteriology. https://doi.org/10.1128/jb.173.14.4254-4262.1991\n\nCatherine L. Squires, Steen B. Pedersen, B. Ross et al. (1991). ClpB is the Escherichia coli heat shock protein F84.1. Journal of Bacteriology. https://doi.org/10.1128/jb.173.14.4254-4262.1991--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nClpB Is the Escherichia coli Heat Shock Protein F84.1 - University of Copenhagen Research Portal (https://researchprofiles.ku.dk/en/publications/clpb-is-the-escherichia-coli-heat-shock-protein-f841/)\nciteturn17search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; Squires, CL, Pedersen, S, Ross, BM & Squires, C 1991, 'ClpB Is the Escherichia coli Heat Shock Protein F84.1', J.\n\n# ClpB Is the Escherichia coli Heat Shock Protein F84.1\n\nC.L. Squires, Steen Pedersen, B.M. Ross, C. Squires\n\nResearch output: Contribution to journal › Journal article › Research\n\nOriginal language  | English\nJourn